# Memory Bank Protocol

This project uses a **Memory Bank** in `memory-bank/` for persistent context across sessions.

## Session start (required)
Before planning or implementing non-trivial work:
1. Read `memory-bank/activeContext.md` and `memory-bank/progress.md`.
2. If touching architecture or dependencies, also read `memory-bank/systemPatterns.md` and `memory-bank/techContext.md`.

## After completing a task (required)
Update the Memory Bank before ending your turn:
1. **`activeContext.md`** — current focus, what changed this session, concrete next steps.
2. **`progress.md`** — mark completed items, add blockers/issues, append a dated changelog entry.
3. **`systemPatterns.md`** — only if folder structure, patterns, or conventions changed.
4. **`techContext.md`** — only if packages, tooling, or dev setup changed.
5. **`projectbrief.md`** / **`productContext.md`** — only if scope, goals, or UX/product decisions changed.

Keep entries factual and concise. Use checkboxes in `progress.md`. Do not duplicate `.cursorrules` — reference it for coding standards.

## File map
| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `projectbrief.md` | Scope, goals, constraints |
| `productContext.md` | Users, UX, product rationale |
| `systemPatterns.md` | Architecture and code patterns |
| `techContext.md` | Stack and environment |
| `activeContext.md` | Now / next (highest churn) |
| `progress.md` | Done / backlog / issues |

See `memory-bank/README.md` for the full workflow.
